# /opt/vpntunnel/vpntunnel.env — runtime flags for the vpntunnel systemd unit.
#
# systemd EnvironmentFile syntax: KEY=value, one per line, no quotes, no spaces
# around '='. This file is OPERATOR-MANAGED: copy it to /opt/vpntunnel/vpntunnel.env
# once and edit by hand. The release workflow does NOT rewrite it — the CI deploy
# user cannot write the base dir, and the values are stable across deploys because
# the unit's ExecStart points at the fixed bin/release channel symlink. It holds
# no secrets (only paths and a hostname). systemd (root) reads it before launching
# the service and passes the values as the process environment, so the service
# user never reads this file: keep it root:root 0600. EnvironmentFile is re-read on
# every restart, so a change here needs only `systemctl restart vpntunnel`, no
# daemon-reload.
#
# VPNTUNNEL_TLS_CERT_DIR must be non-empty in production — an empty value runs
# the API as plain HTTP (the post-deploy HTTPS health-check would then fail).
VPNTUNNEL_CONFIG_PATH=/opt/vpntunnel/configs/proxy.json
VPNTUNNEL_TLS_CERT_DIR=/opt/vpntunnel/configs/tls/
VPNTUNNEL_TLS_CERT_HOST=localhost
